---
/**
 * Brief §7: short. Who runs That AI, the "amplify, not replace" thesis in two paragraphs, and the
 * fact that we build with AI ourselves and test everything we ship.
 * No stock imagery, no team grid.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="That AI builds working AI-assisted systems for small and growth-stage operators that have real revenue and no in-house technical team."
>
  <div class="u-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="about u-measure-wide">
      <p class="about__lead">
        That AI Consultancy builds working AI-assisted systems for small and growth-stage operators
        that have real revenue and no in-house technical team.
      </p>

      <p>
        We do not replace people — we amplify them. The businesses we work with already know their
        trade better than any software vendor does. What they lack is the layer between the platforms
        they run and the way they actually work: the part that means a price is entered once rather
        than twice, or that an idea can be shown to a developer rather than described to one. That
        layer is what we build.
      </p>

      <p>
        It follows that we are a consultancy that happens to specialise in intelligent automation,
        not an AI startup. We are not trying to move your team onto our product. We connect what you
        already run, we tell you when a thing cannot be built on the platforms you own, and we say so
        before you have paid anyone to try.
      </p>

      <p>
        We build with AI ourselves, throughout — which is why integration-grade work fits a
        small-operator budget. That is a reason to be more careful, not less: we measure how a
        platform actually behaves before building against it, we preview every change offline before
        it touches a client-facing page, and we test everything we ship. Where a platform is
        ambiguous, our systems under-match rather than guess.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-block">
      <Cta />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding-block: var(--space-20) var(--space-10);
  }

  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .about__lead {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: var(--lead-snug);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-snug);
  }

  .cta-block {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--section-y);
  }
</style>
